{"t": 999.1, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 4, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_Doubler_Zener", "rationale": "The previous best design (SSHI_FullBridge_Zener) failed only on S3 ripple (61mV vs 50mV) and S5 settled (22mV vs 20mV), both very close to the limits. I am replacing the full-bridge rectifier with a voltage-doubler (Greinacher) stage. This topology is often more efficient at low excitation (S4) and provides a higher voltage headroom, which may reduce the relative output ripple. The Zener DZ33 will maintain the output within the 1.8-3.6V range, while the SSHI flip increases the total available energy. This structural change should shift the ripple and settling characteristics enough to pass all conditions.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_Doubler_Zener", "rationale": "The previous best design (SSHI_FullBridge_Zener) failed only on S3 ripple (61mV vs 50mV) and S5 settled (22mV vs 20mV), both very close to the limits. I am replacing the full-bridge rectifier with a voltage-doubler (Greinacher) stage. This topology is often more efficient at low excitation (S4) and provides a higher voltage headroom, which may reduce the relative output ripple. The Zener DZ33 will maintain the output within the 1.8-3.6V range, while the SSHI flip increases the total available energy. This structural change should shift the ripple and settling characteristics enough to pass all conditions.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n_flip"], "value": 0.0047}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n_flip", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 2e-05, "phase": 0.1, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "n_pump"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C_pump", "type": "C", "nodes": ["n_pump", "0"], "value": 1e-07}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n_pump", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes"